abstract: >
  Definition note for the term oncoclastics: the application of hazard-exposure-vulnerability-resilience
  assessment, as developed in disaster-risk reduction, to the fragmentation of cancer-related trajectories,
  in two senses (biological and care-system). Maps the Risk Mechanism Theory Index (RMTI) domains onto both
  senses and includes a small tested Python module that scores them through the unchanged RMTI core.
  Research framework: not validated against real outcomes; not a medical device.
